terraform from start to backend setup (my notes)

i started by installing terraform and aws cli on my mac
terraform is used to create infrastructure using code
aws cli is used to connect my local system with aws account

first i checked aws cli using command
aws --version

then i connected aws using
aws configure

i entered:

access key

secret key

region ap-south-1

output json

this step connects my system to aws

after that i created a folder
mkdir terraform-new
cd terraform-new

then i created a file
vim terraform.tf

inside this file i wrote provider block

provider "aws" {
region = "ap-south-1"
}

this tells terraform which cloud and region to use

then i created my first resource (ec2 instance)

resource "aws_instance" "my_ec2" {
ami = "ami-xxxxxxxx"
instance_type = "t2.micro"
}

then i ran

terraform init

this downloads required plugins and prepares terraform

then i ran

terraform plan

this shows what terraform will create

then

terraform apply

this actually created ec2 instance on aws

after that i created s3 bucket using terraform

resource "aws_s3_bucket" "my_bucket" {
bucket = "rashpal-terraform-bucket-12345"
}

i applied again and bucket was created

problem i faced
when bucket already existed terraform showed error
so i used

terraform import aws_s3_bucket.my_bucket rashpal-terraform-bucket-12345

this command connects existing resource with terraform

then i learned about state file

terraform creates a file called terraform.tfstate
this file stores all infrastructure details

problem:
if this file is local → not safe for team use

solution:
use remote backend

for remote backend i used s3 + dynamodb

s3 is used to store state file
dynamodb is used for locking

locking means:
only one person can run terraform at a time

i already had s3 bucket so i used that

then i created dynamodb table

resource "aws_dynamodb_table" "tf_lock" {
name = "terraform-lock"
billing_mode = "PAY_PER_REQUEST"
hash_key = "LockID"

attribute {
name = "LockID"
type = "S"
}
}

then applied it

after that i added backend block

terraform {
backend "s3" {
bucket = "rashpal-terraform-bucket-12345"
key = "dev/terraform.tfstate"
region = "ap-south-1"
dynamodb_table = "terraform-lock"
}
}

this tells terraform:
store state in s3
use dynamodb for locking

then i ran

terraform init

it asked to copy state → i typed yes

now my state moved from local to s3

verification

i checked s3 bucket
i saw terraform.tfstate file

i checked dynamodb table
it was empty normally

when i run terraform apply
a lock item appears and disappears

final understanding

terraform → creates infrastructure
aws cli → connects local system to aws
provider → defines cloud
resource → defines what to create
state file → stores infra data
s3 → stores state remotely
dynamodb → locks state